      <Docs>
        <summary>
          <para>The caller tried to execute a function that does not exist.</para>
          <para>This error is returned to the caller of AppFunctionManager.executeAppFunction if one of the following is true: The function identifier specified in ExecuteAppFunctionRequest.getFunctionIdentifier does not match any function identifiers in the metadata returned by AppFunctionManager.searchAppFunctions; The app function is AppFunctionMetadata.SCOPE_ACTIVITY and ExecuteAppFunctionRequest.getActivityId is not provided or does not match any activity identifiers returned by AppFunctionState.getActivityIds, this error will be returned; The app function is AppFunctionMetadata.SCOPE_GLOBAL and ExecuteAppFunctionRequest.getActivityId is non-null.</para>
          <para>This error is in the ERROR_CATEGORY_REQUEST_ERROR category.</para>
          <para><format type="text/html"><a href="https://developer.android.com/reference/android/app/appfunctions/AppFunctionException#ERROR_FUNCTION_NOT_FOUND" title="Reference documentation">Android reference for <code>android.app.appfunctions.AppFunctionException.ERROR_FUNCTION_NOT_FOUND</code>.</a></format></para>
